---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import Note from '../../components/Note.astro';
---

<Page path="reference/variables">
<section id="labels">
  <h2 id="all"><a href="#all">What a universe passes</a></h2>
  <p>A compose file describes how it is reached with labels, read with <code>docker compose config</code>. The key names the host, the value is the container port:</p>
  <Terminal><pre><span class="k">services</span>:
  <span class="k">app-dev</span>:
    <span class="k">labels</span>:
      <span class="k">dev.multiversectl.host.app</span>: "4200"              <span class="c"># app-u3.&lt;domain&gt; -> port 4200</span>
      <span class="k">dev.multiversectl.host.api</span>: "8001"
      <span class="k">dev.multiversectl.host.api.entrypoint</span>: devapi   <span class="c"># default: web</span>
      <span class="k">dev.multiversectl.host.api.aliases</span>: app,adm     <span class="c"># same service, other hostnames</span>
      <span class="k">dev.multiversectl.host.api.portForward</span>: auto    <span class="c"># also at &lt;ip&gt;:&lt;free port&gt;</span>
      <span class="k">dev.multiversectl.publish</span>: "true"               <span class="c"># keep my published ports</span></pre></Terminal>
  <Note><p><strong>No labels needed in the common case.</strong> A service that exposes exactly one port is reached at the app's own name: app <code>ui</code> becomes <code>ui-u3.&lt;domain&gt;</code>. Ambiguity (several services with ports, or one service with several ports) is an error that names the exact label to add.</p></Note>
  <p>Order of precedence, per app: <code>hosts:</code> in the manifest, then <code>dev.multiversectl.host.*</code> labels, then the single exposed port.</p>
  <h4>Variables</h4>
  <p>Available to compose files and inline overlays:</p>
  <div class="tw"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variable</th><th scope="col">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr><td data-l="Key"><code>UNIVERSE, UNIVERSE_SLUG, UNIVERSE_DIR</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">The number (<code>3</code>), the slug (<code>u3</code>), and the universe's directory.</td></tr><tr><td data-l="Key"><code>MULTIVERSE_DOMAIN</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">The wildcard domain in use.</td></tr><tr><td data-l="Key"><code>MULTIVERSE_ROOT, MULTIVERSE_PROJECT</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">The multiverse's root directory (the clones and <code>universes/</code> are under it) and its name, for a script or an agent that has only the environment.</td></tr><tr><td data-l="Key"><code>COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">The universe's compose project.</td></tr><tr><td data-l="Key"><code>&lt;HOST&gt;_HOST</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">One per host key, e.g. <code>APP_HOST</code> is <code>app-u3.&lt;domain&gt;</code>.</td></tr><tr><td data-l="Key"><code>&lt;REPO&gt;_DIR</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">One per repository: that repository's checkout in the universe.</td></tr><tr><td data-l="Key"><code>HOST_UID, HOST_GID</code></td><td data-l="Meaning">The current user; a <code>spec.env</code> entry overrides them.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
</section>
</Page>
